Yes, that is an accepted English word:

leitmotif or leitmotiv noun 1 a theme or image, etc which recurs throughout 
a piece of music, novel, etc. 2 music in musical dramas, especially 
Wagnerian ones: a short piece of music that is always associated with a 
particular person, idea, feeling, etc.

ETYMOLOGY: 19c: German Leitmotiv, from leiten to lead + Motiv motif.

(from http://www.chambersharrap.co.uk/chambers/chref/chref.py/main?query=leitmotif&title=21st)

